Problem Validation collaboration
Textbook pricing is predatory and the cheaper option is never offered by the university a student is at. 
A solution to this problem is to create a deal aggregator that focuses on free resources and third party markets. 
If its a website, it must also act as a trusted middle man who verifies sellers and other websites that offer textbooks.
University pricing will be the basis of success. To determine success of the deals aggregator, buyer survey data must be collected.
Ask "Have you purchased literature for classes that is cheaper than a university bookstore?"
Trustworthyness can be developed through a "corporative."

Inputs: University bookstore price comparison, and third party sellers(students).
Outputs: Online deals aggregator that actively tracks prices from universities, and acts as a trusted middle man between buyers
and sellers in the third party market.
Solution Criteria: Reviewers who acknowledge that they saved money through the website.

